{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y8mb9PwEfLSCRdu4PdWVfL","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2023 Review Guidelines Analysis\n\nBased on my review of the provided content, I must report that **the specific numeric scoring scales are not included in this document**.\n\n## What IS Present:\n\nThe guidelines specify six review dimensions that reviewers must evaluate:\n\n1. \"Originality\" - novelty and differentiation from prior work\n2. \"Quality\" - technical soundness and evidence support\n3. \"Clarity\" - writing quality and organization\n4. \"Significance\" - importance and state-of-art advancement\n5. \"Relevance\" - alignment with robot learning focus\n6. \"Limitations\" - honest assessment of shortcomings\n\n## What IS NOT Present:\n\nThe document does not contain:\n- Numeric scoring scales (e.g., 1-10, 1-5)\n- Overall recommendation scales with values\n- Confidence level scales\n- Specific point ranges for each dimension\n\nThe guidelines emphasize qualitative evaluation criteria and constructive feedback principles but reference external resources (ICML and NeurIPS guidelines) for detailed scoring instructions without reproducing their scales in this excerpt."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"808481c6-6a8a-4eae-a76b-0f8df33193a6","uuid":"3c54c4e5-56fe-40c7-92aa-88bc11081d1d","timestamp":"2026-05-16T08:36:07.963Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":105095,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2023 Review Guidelines Analysis\n\nBased on my review of the provided content, I must report that **the specific numeric scoring scales are not included in this document**.\n\n## What IS Present:\n\nThe guidelines specify six review dimensions that reviewers must evaluate:\n\n1. \"Originality\" - novelty and differentiation from prior work\n2. \"Quality\" - technical soundness and evidence support\n3. \"Clarity\" - writing quality and organization\n4. \"Significance\" - importance and state-of-art advancement\n5. \"Relevance\" - alignment with robot learning focus\n6. \"Limitations\" - honest assessment of shortcomings\n\n## What IS NOT Present:\n\nThe document does not contain:\n- Numeric scoring scales (e.g., 1-10, 1-5)\n- Overall recommendation scales with values\n- Confidence level scales\n- Specific point ranges for each dimension\n\nThe guidelines emphasize qualitative evaluation criteria and constructive feedback principles but reference external resources (ICML and NeurIPS guidelines) for detailed scoring instructions without reproducing their scales in this excerpt.","durationMs":4676,"url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"}}
